# tests/MANIFEST -- how each SQL suite is run by scripts/run_suites.{sh,ps1}
#
# One line per suite that needs anything other than the default. The default
# is: a virgin copy of the head database, the suite's own pass|fail summary
# row decides, and a suite printing no summary row is NO RESULT (informational).
#
#   suite          key=value ...
#
# Keys
#   era=NNNN       run against a database built only up to migration NNNN.
#                  For acceptance suites written for one migration whose
#                  assertions describe THAT moment ("policy count is 105",
#                  "v_price_check has 20 columns") and are meaningless later.
#                  This is not a relaxation: the suite still runs, at the level
#                  it was written for, and must pass there.
#   requires=NNNN  skip, with a printed reason, unless the database is at or
#                  beyond NNNN. For acceptance suites of a migration that may
#                  still be in proposed/.
#   seq=NAME       part of an ordered group that shares ONE database copy, in
#                  file order, because later members read what earlier ones
#                  created.
#   rows           the suite prints result rows without a summary; count any
#                  row whose verdict column reads FAIL as a failure instead of
#                  treating the suite as NO RESULT.
#   skip=REASON    never run automatically.
#
# Anything not listed runs at head on a virgin copy.

